/*!
    \page vscodeext-how-preview-qml.html
    \previouspage vscodeext-how-tos.html
    \nextpage vscodeext-reference.html

    \ingroup vscodeext-how-to-qml

    \title Preview Qt Quick applications

    You can preview Qt Quick applications and single QML files from the code
    editor. The changes you make to the code become instantly visible in the
    preview.

    \image {vscodeext-qml-preview.gif} {Previewing a Qt Quick application}
    \caption Previewing a Qt Quick application.

    \section1 Preview the whole application

    To launch and preview a Qt Quick application:

    \list 1
        \li To launch the application:
            \list
                \li Select \inlineimage {preview-app.png} {Preview changes to QML code live in your application}
                    on the editor toolbar.
                \li Go to \uicontrol {Command Palette}, and select
                    \uicontrol {Qt: Preview changes to QML code live in your application}.
            \endlist
        \li Select the application executable as the launch target.
    \endlist

    If the build directory is outside the workspace, select
    \uicontrol {Qt: Open Qt Extension settings} > \uicontrol {Qt QML Configuration}
    to set it in \uicontrol {Preview: Additional Build Dirs}. This tells \QVSC
    where to look for QRC files during QML preview.

    To pass command-line arguments to the application when you start it from the
    command palette, set them in \uicontrol {Qt: Open Qt Extension settings} >
    \uicontrol {Qt QML Configuration} > \uicontrol {Preview: Args}.

    \section1 Preview a single file

    To preview a single QML file:

    \list
        \li Select \inlineimage {preview-file.png} {Preview current QML file live}
            on the editor toolbar.
        \li Go to \uicontrol {Command Palette}, and select
            \uicontrol {Qt: Preview current QML file live}.
    \endlist

    \section1 Attach to a running application for live preview

    To Attach to a running Qt Quick application for live preview:

    \list 1
        \li In the \uicontrol Terminal, start the application with the following
            arguments:
            \badcode
            <your_executable_path> -qmljsdebugger=host:<IP_address>,port:<port_number>,block,services:QmlPreview,DebugTranslation
            \endcode
            Where \e IP_address is the IP address of the host where the
            application is running and \e port_number is the debugging port.
        \li Go to \uicontrol {Command Palette}, and select
            \uicontrol {Qt: Attach to a running QML application for live preview}.
        \li Enter the IP address where the application is running.
        \li Enter the port number where the application is running.
    \endlist

    \section1 Stop previewing

    To stop previewing a Qt Quick application or a QML file:

    \list
        \li Close the preview window.
        \li Select \inlineimage {stop-circle.png} {Stop QML preview} on the
            editor toolbar.
    \endlist

    \sa {Qt settings}
*/
